const YEARBOOK_WEAKNESSES={"Atron":"Web/kiting variants have poor damage and tank; blaster fits struggle against ships not vulnerable to Atron’s falloff/control tactic.","Condor":"Kiting avoids anti-kiters; scram-kite variant has weaker tank and damage, so leave if losing the DPS race.","Executioner":"Weak tank and only 3 mids make positional advantage important; scram-kite has less tank/damage and poor Scorch performance.","Slasher":"Weak tank and poor damage; relies heavily on speed and EWAR. Kiting damage is weak and intentions can be obvious.","Breacher":"Rage has poor application with one web, forcing faction ammo and lower damage; the two-web version sacrifices a lot of tank.","Incursus":"Low speed and no falloff bonus give poor range control; damage falls quickly with range and alternatives are less flexible.","Kestrel":"Two-web fits trade away tank/damage; the hull is slow with poor capacitor, making solo kiting poor and positional advantage important.","Merlin":"Very slow and struggles against prepared scram/web kiters; rail fits are off-meta and it relies heavily on positional advantage.","Punisher":"Only 2 mids limits range control and web application; slow, with weak projection for solo kiting and blaster fits.","Rifter":"150mm brawl fit has poor damage at scram range; artillery fit has weaker capacitor because it lacks tackle-cap reduction.","Tormentor":"Power creep left it behind; beam fit has weaker control/tracking issues, while pulse fit is poor against blaster brawlers and has little hull buffer.","Tristan":"Poor damage in brawl and poor control in kite/scram-kite due to low speed and only 3 mids; generally worse than specialised frigates.","Caldari Navy Hookbill":"Damage is effectively kinetic-locked; EWAR fits are weak against drone frigates, while tank-focused variants give up control.","Federation Navy Comet":"Main weakness is control: only 3 mids means double-web fits can control it; rail fits often need a neut against tracking-mitigation fits.","Imperial Navy Slicer":"Very weak capacitor requires careful MWD/disruptor management; beam kiting has poor tracking and is harder to manage.","Republic Fleet Firetail":"Artillery has bad turret tracking and needs more precise piloting; brawling is outclassed by Comet, though more flexible.","Crucifier Navy Issue":"Overshadowed by Comet/Hookbill; beam fit gains little extra control versus common double-web Navy frigates, while Scorch scram-kite damage is poor.","Griffin Navy Issue":"Terrible base speed leaves it behind two-web control; positional advantage matters and ECM outcomes retain randomness.","Maulus Navy Issue":"Kiting fit is too slow; scram-kite is weak on tank×DPS versus Navy frigates; neut fit offers too little value over cheaper Tristan.","Vigil Fleet Issue":"No major weakness is singled out; web-kite is strongest in position, while fit choices trade tank, control and damage.","Heron Navy Issue":"Lower tank, speed and damage than stronger Navy scram-kiters; LML kite is held back by poor top speed and competition from Probe Fleet.","Imicus Navy Issue":"Worse damage, tank and speed than Comet; extra web gives only slightly better control because of slower speed/agility, and rail fit is subpar.","Magnate Navy Issue":"Baseline scram-kite has less control than Navy Crucifier; kiting range is worse than Slicer and needs drugs to become acceptable.","Probe Fleet Issue":"Rocket fit cannot web-kite, so it relies on neuts and careful capacitor management; overall control is more constrained than Vigil Fleet.","Astero":"Very poor damage despite unavoidable drones; expensive for its performance and relies on tank/control. Loses when it cannot tank the opponent.","Cruor":"Mediocre damage and tank without capacitor warfare; poor performance per cost and relies on neuts/nos to create its win condition.","Damavik":"Slow and dependent on neuts/range control; short fights are bad because disintegrator spool is valuable over time. AB fit is hard-countered by kiters/web kiters.","Daredevil":"Blaster fits out of position struggle against stronger scram-kiters; rail fits require a good faction web and positional advantage.","Dramiel":"No unique combat bonuses; autocannon fit has to trade between brawling and scram-kiting, while artillery fits have no exceptional raw stats and need good piloting.","Garmur":"High-end kite fits are expensive; cheaper fits need defensive scram because tackle range/speed are worse. Rocket variant needs two webs to apply Rage fully.","Metamorphosis":"Jack-of-all-trades but worse than specialised Navy frigates; usually cannot beat ships stronger than Navy frigates/T1 destroyers and has poor price/performance.","Skybreaker":"Weak damage and poor performance per cost make it unsuitable for many solo fights; relies on range because close-range damage is weak.","Succubus":"Neither tank nor damage is great; pulse scram-kite with Scorch is no longer competitive and usually needs polarized brawling instead.","Worm":"Poor control is its major weakness; it cannot pin many targets in scram range and is relatively slow for a kiter.","Enyo":"Poor control is the key weakness; blaster fit dislikes scram kiters and tracking disruptors, while rail kite is weaker than several other AFs.","Harpy":"Weak damage bonus makes blaster DPS races difficult; rail fits suffer poor control/damage/slot layout. Tracking disruptors and neuts are strong counters.","Hawk":"Slower and shield-locked, so it cannot match Hookbill control; two-MASB fit is vulnerable to control issues, while one-MASB gives up much tank.","Ishkur":"Strong active tank comes with poor control; if you cannot break the tank, leave. Neuting fit is rare and not strong against its normal engagement profile.","Jaguar":"Scram-kite variant is generally worse than Hawk because damage/range matter more; anti-kite fit loses to most brawlers/scram-kiters due to weak tank/DPS and has a narrow profile.","Nergal":"Very expensive; short optimal and vulnerability to getting scrammed at warp-ins. MWD fit has control problems versus MWD frigates/multiple opponents; brawl fit is polarising.","Retribution":"Locked into kiting by its 2 mids; brawling lacks control and is vulnerable to neuts/TDs. Beam kiting is more popular because it can sustain the cap load.","Vengeance":"Poor damage is the biggest weakness; no range bonus and Rage does not cover the whole scram-kite range. Two-rep fit is countered by web kiters/kiters.","Wolf":"Poor DPS, abysmal projection and worst tank among AF kiters; brawl fit has only 2 mids, letting opponents escape, and kinetic resist is a common target.","Claw":"The Yearbook lists the ship and tier but does not provide a dedicated profile/commentary page, so no ship-specific weakness is stated.","Crusader":"The Yearbook lists the ship and tier but does not provide a dedicated profile/commentary page, so no ship-specific weakness is stated.","Raptor":"The Yearbook lists the ship and tier but does not provide a dedicated profile/commentary page, so no ship-specific weakness is stated.","Taranis":"The Yearbook lists the ship and tier but does not provide a dedicated profile/commentary page, so no ship-specific weakness is stated."};

